## Task granularity and design freedom

The external contract is fixed; language, runtime, process topology, build,
executable layout, and component boundaries remain design variables unless an
authoritative input restricts them. Scope limits uncertainty, not diff size.

Return one stable hypothesis with causal claim, activation evidence, falsifier,
analytical effect range, the bar, and a causally complete
task. Keep the handoff under 4,000 output tokens: {{ reply.invariants }} cites stable files
and adds only hypothesis diagnostics; {{ reply.task }} states the component/interface and
stages without an exhaustive shell recipe; {{ reply.pass_criteria }} adds only activation,
correctness, cleanup, and evidence gates; {{ reply.reasoning }} gives the decisive
comparison and rejected alternatives briefly. Also give a short {{ reply.title }}.

Include in {{ reply.task }} a verification strategy: the cheapest checks the implementer
should run before declaring the work done. These are not exhaustive test plans;
they are the minimum steps that exercise the failure-prone path (e.g. "confirm
the image builds," "hit /health and get 200," "run the accuracy checker against
the live endpoint"). Adapt the strategy across retries based on what failed.

The implementer reads a trusted evaluation only as its reply states it: each stage's
verdict, its metric values and the end of its summary, and the comparison with the base. It
cannot read the benchmark's server or process logs, raw outputs or profiler captures, and its
editor may have no accelerator. {{ reply.pass_criteria }} and {{ reply.activation_evidence }}
that need such data (a report quoting log lines, a table computed from them) can never be
met: the implementer reports blocked and the round ends without a measurement. Require only
what it can read, and measure what needs the logs through the next round's evaluation.

Stage cost: cheap capability, comparable point, then expand past noise.
Stop on fair falsification; reuse plumbing/rows. Evaluations have no allowance
to plan for or against. The framework owns the trusted gates, the base, review
cadence, and terminal detection.
After a correctness failure, cover changed dataflow locally or stagewise isolate
defects before another target call; leaf-only checks do not suffice.

